WEBVTT

00:00:21.403 --> 00:00:27.660
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> In most towns and cities round the world, the high streets are full of chain stores.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:33.980
Here are some of the most popular global chain stores on our high streets now.

00:00:36.792 --> 00:00:39.300
Zara is a Spanish fashion chain.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:43.700
It is now one of the biggest clothes companies in the world.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:51.580
<i>Fun fact! Zara can create and distribute a new design in less than two weeks.</i>

00:01:01.185 --> 00:01:03.820
H&amp;M is a Swedish clothes chain.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:07.620
It sells quality clothes at a very good price.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:15.611
<i>Fun fact! H&amp;M employees always celebrate the opening of a new store with a dance.</i>

00:01:24.047 --> 00:01:28.380
A lot of people think that Uniqlo is quite a new clothing chain,

00:01:28.511 --> 00:01:32.820
but it actually started in Japan in 1949.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:38.540
<i>Fun fact! Uniqlo sells 50 different colours of socks.</i>

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:52.460
Nike is an American chain that sells sports clothes and shoes.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:57.140
It sells more than 900 million items every year.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:04.648
<i>Fun fact! The Nike symbol has its own name – it’s called the ‘Swoosh’.</i>

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:17.940
The first Body Shop opened in Brighton, England, in 1976.

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:24.060
It sells environmentally-friendly products for the body, face, hair, and home.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:31.820
<i>Fun fact! The first Body Shop was painted dark green, not to be more eco-friendly,</i>

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:38.180
<i>but because the shop had a lot of mould and dark green was the only colour that could cover it.</i>

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:54.300
Apple is an American technology company, selling phones, tablets, and computers.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:03:02.683
<i>Fun fact! Apple launched a clothing line in 1986, which didn’t have any success.</i>

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.860
Chains are popular because they are familiar –

00:03:15.409 --> 00:03:19.780
if we go to a new town or even to a different country,

00:03:20.123 --> 00:03:24.900
we know that we can find our favourite products in these shops.